1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Today we will look at B-trees, a data structure designed for efficient disk access.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Each node stores several keys. This keeps the tree shallow even when the dataset grows.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Searching a balanced B-tree takes logarithmic time in the number of stored keys.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:34,000
When a node becomes full during insertion, we split it and promote the middle key.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,000
The split preserves balance. Every leaf stays at the same depth.

